     },
     "kind": "estimate",
     "literals": [],
     "text": "The other $2,598,315 is raised and never needed; it reaches free cash a year or two later, not the year it was raised."
    }
   ],
   "rests_on": [
    "b-l",
    "b-raised",
    "b-paid",
    "b-lapsed"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "Budgeting the cushion raises taxes for money that, in most years, is never needed for special education."
   },
   "text": "Added to the budget every year, $224,310 raises $3,813,270 over 17 years to pay $1,214,955 of overspending."
  },
  {
   "figures": {
    "a": {
     "text": "$1,439,265",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 1439265
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "$224,310",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 224310
    }
   },
   "literals": [],
   "rests_on": [
    "b-res",
    "b-l",
    "b-paid"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "A reserve asks taxpayers once, and afterwards only for what was actually used."
   },
   "text": "Held once as a reserve, the same protection raises $1,439,265: $224,310 up front, then refills."
  },
  {
   "figures": {
    "a": {
     "text": "$452,580",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 452580.0
    }
   },
   "literals": [
    "1",
    "2024"
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "cite": {
      "href": "/docs/meetings/text/select-board/2025-10-07-minutes-7441.txt",
      "label": "Select Board minutes, 2025-10-07"
     },
     "figures": {},
     "kind": "quote",
     "literals": [],
     "text": "A reserve cannot be moved that way: spending it needs a majority of both the School Committee and the Select Board."
    }
   ],
   "rests_on": [
    "b-moved"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "Money in a budget line protects nothing if it can be moved out before the bill arrives."
   },
   "text": "A cushion in the budget can be moved: on 1 July 2024, $452,580 left out-of-district tuition."
  },
  {
   "figures": {
    "a": {
     "text": "11",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 11
    },
    "n": {
     "text": "17",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 17
    }
   },
   "literals": [],
   "notes": [
    {
     "figures": {},
     "kind": "estimate",
     "literals": [],
     "text": "So a reserve replaces the cushion in the budget rather than adding to it, if the budget is set lower once the reserve exists (our reading)."
    }
   ],
   "rests_on": [
    "b-under",
    "b-cush"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "A reserve saves money only if the budget is set lower once it exists: that is the decision to watch."
   },
   "text": "The cushion is already there: the three lines spent under budget in 11 of 17 years."
  }
 ],
